' One remainder binding merges in place, all or nothing (DR-103 part 2,
' Phase D item D-D1b). handle_remainder charges one search, then merges the
' binding at the level. An existing binding is merged in place. A new binding
' starts as an empty Par; it is inserted only after its merge and its insert
' reservation succeed. Every merger reserves before it assigns, so each
' rejection leaves the free map unchanged, and the callers can backtrack.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-103);
'                  rholang/src/rust/interpreter/matcher/list_match.rs
'                  (handle_remainder); spatial_matcher.rs (merge_set_remainder,
'                  merge_map_remainder).
' Formal model:    formal/rocq/cost_accounted_rho/theories/FreeMapBindings.v
'                  (part 2: in_place_merge_equals_copy_merge,
'                  rejected_merge_leaves_map).
' Palette:  charges = gate teal · merger = process lilac · new binding = delta amber
'           accepted state = pool green · rejection = reject red · input = supply blue
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/remainder-in-place-merge.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh remainder-in-place-merge.puml)

@startuml remainder-in-place-merge
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_control
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor $ca_note_red
skinparam NoteBorderColor #666666
title One remainder binding merges in place, all or nothing (DR-103 part 2)

start
:handle_remainder(targets, level, merger)\nthe targets come from charged copies with their cleanup; <<$ca_supply>>
:reserve one free-map search\n<latex>S(n) = 11 \cdot h(n)</latex> operations and <latex>8\,S(n)</latex> scanned bytes; <<$ca_gate>>
:reserve one operation for the merger's work context; <<$ca_gate>>
if (is a binding b stored at the level?) then (yes)
  :merger(b, targets) changes b in place:\nall reservations first, then the assignments; <<$ca_process>>
  if (does a reservation reject?) then (yes)
    :return None\nb is unchanged, so the free map is unchanged; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :b holds the merged binding\nno copy of b and no drop of b; <<$ca_pool>>
  endif
else (no)
  :b ← an empty Par; <<$ca_delta>>
  :merger(b, targets); <<$ca_process>>
  if (does a reservation reject?) then (yes)
    :return None\nb is dropped, and the free map is unchanged; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :reserve the insert (DR-103 part 1):\nthe search, <latex>h(n+1) \cdot L</latex> moves and the growth <latex>B(n+1) - B(n)</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
    if (does the insert reservation reject?) then (yes)
      :return None\nthe free map is unchanged; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
      stop
    else (no)
      :insert b at the level; <<$ca_pool>>
    endif
  endif
endif
:return Some(()); <<$ca_pool>>
note right
  Before DR-103 part 2: copy b with a charged copy and
  cleanup of the whole binding, merge the copy, reserve
  the insert and insert the copy again. A Par remainder
  merges ten field lists into one binding, so its growing
  binding was copied up to ten times.
end note
stop

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| input of the merge |
  |<$ca_gate>| host-work reservation |
  |<$ca_process>| merger (reservations, then assignments) |
  |<$ca_delta>| new binding |
  |<$ca_pool>| accepted state |
  |<$ca_rejectfill>| rejection: the free map is unchanged |
endlegend
@enduml
